cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use RESIDUDES — residudes, residudes-engine, residudes-qa — or the residudes-decoy pool, please cite the CASP17 abstract below."
title: "Protein Complex Structure Prediction with RESIDUDES in CASP17"
abstract: >-
  The DeepFold team's CASP17 entry (group 077, RESIDUDES-X): residudes, a campaign agent that takes a
  target from its sequence to a slate of five models and stops wherever a person has to approve;
  residudes-engine, which builds the inputs and runs Protenix v2, OpenFold 3, Boltz-2 and AlphaFold 3;
  and residudes-qa, which scores, clusters and plots the pool. The sampling pool itself is released as
  residudes-decoy.
type: software
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/DeepFoldProtein/RESIDUDES"
url: "https://lantern-decoy.deepfold.org"
keywords:
  - CASP17
  - protein structure prediction
  - protein complexes
  - model selection
  - AlphaFold 3
